file.content:
[
  {
    "id": "c001",
    "name": "Preamble and Agreement",
    "text": "This Distribution Agreement is made effective as of the lst day of January, 2009, between Kellogg Sales Company, a Delaware corporation, dba Kellogg Snacks, One Kellogg Square, Battle Creek, Michigan 49016 hereinafter referred to as “COMPANY” and Two Locks, Inc. d/b/a Premier Snack Distributors, with offices at 50 Rose Place, Garden City Park, New York 11040 hereinafter referred to as “DISTRIBUTOR,” (“Agreement”) as further defined below.” For good and valuable consideration of the terms and conditions contained herein, the parties hereby do agree as follows:"
  },
  {
    "id": "c002",
    "name": "1(i). DISTRIBUTOR(s)",
    "text": "1, DEFINITIONS (i) DISTRIBUTOR(s) when performing hereunder shall be an independent contractor and shall transact all business pursuant to this Agreement on its own behalf and for its own account. DISTRIBUTOR has no power or authority to act as agent or otherwise for the account or on behalf of COMPANY. Neither DISTRIBUTOR nor its employees/agents shall be considered employees of COMPANY, and neither party shall in any event be held liable or accountable for any obligations incurred by either party other than as specified herein, it being specifically understood that the respective businesses of each of the parties shall be operated separate and apart from each other. Neither DISTRIBUTOR nor any of its employees/agent shall represent that it or they are employees of COMPANY."
  },
  {
    "id": "c003",
    "name": "1(ii). Product(s)",
    "text": "(ii) Product(s) PRODUCT or PRODUCTS shall mean only those products authorized by COMPANY for sale to DISTRIBUTOR. COMPANY will provide pricing for each of the PRODUCTS. COMPANY reserves the right to eliminate any PRODUCT for any reason."
  },
  {
    "id": "c004",
    "name": "1(iii). Territory",
    "text": "(iii) Territory TERRITORY shall mean the authorized geographic areas for distribution designated as such on Exhibit “A” attached hereto and incorporated herein. DISTRIBUTOR is authorized to sell PRODUCTS to retail grocery store outlet customers only (with this being the “AUTHORIZED CHANNEL OF TRADE”) within their authorized TERRITORY (“CUSTOMERS”)."
  },
  {
    "id": "c005",
    "name": "1(iv). Good Industry Practice",
    "text": "(iv) | Good Industry Practice Shall mean the standards that have developed and are universally accepted and followed in the baking industry, including, but not limited to, maintaining an adequate and fresh supply of PRODUCTS, properly rotating all PRODUCTS, maintaining all equipment in a sanitary condition and in good safe working order, and maintaining proper service and delivery to all CUSTOMERS requesting service."
  },
  {
    "id": "c006",
    "name": "2. TERM OF AGREEMENT",
    "text": "2. TERM OF AGREEMENT Subject to Section 12 of this Agreement, this Agreement shall become effective as of the date hereof and shall continue until December 31, 2010, and shall continue in effect until either party terminates this agreement by providing the other party with written notice of termination at least ninety (90) days prior to such termination. DISTRIBUTOR shall have the right to enter into consecutive successor DSDD Distributor Agreements unless this (or any applicable successor) Agreement has been terminated or unless DISTRIBUTOR has committed a material breach of this (or any applicable successor) Agreement which remains outstanding as of the date that DISTRIBUTOR notifies COMPANY of its desire to enter into a successor Agreement (as specified below) and which material breach COMPANY has not waived. The term of the first successor DSDD Distributor Agreement shall commence on the date that this Agreement expires, and the term of each successor DSDD Distributor Agreement shall begin on the date that the applicable predecessor DSDD Distributor Agreement expires. If DISTRIBUTOR wishes to exercise its w right to enter into a successor DSDD Distributor Agreements, it will do so by executing COMPANY’S then-current form of DSDD Distributor Agreement, the terms of which may differ from the terms of this Agreement."
  },
  {
    "id": "c007",
    "name": "3(i). COMPANY",
    "text": "3. RIGHTS AND DUTIES OF THE PARTIES (i) COMPANY During the term of this Agreement COMPANY shall determine the TERRITORY and AUTHORIZED CHANNEL OF TRADE for DISTRIBUTOR. COMPANY reserves the right to authorize another distributor; wholesaler or COMPANY’S own sales force to sell PRODUCTS in all or a portion of DISTRIBUTOR’S TERRITORY."
  },
  {
    "id": "c008",
    "name": "3(ii)(a). Permitted sales and in-store service",
    "text": "(ii) DISTRIBUTOR (a) During the term of this Agreement, DISTRIBUTOR shall (and may only) (1) Sell to: A. grocery store retail outlets only Bi Kmart C, specific customers as approved by COMPANY AND (ii) Provide “in-store service” to all individual customers where the COMPANY’S products are sold. These services will consist of, but are not limited to: A. Conducting selling presentations to management of individual stores B. Servicing product on shelves and displays, including building displays, stocking product, rotating product, removing stale and damaged product and other product service related activities Cc, Provide “guaranteed sales” to DISTRIBUTOR’S customers defined as providing a credit to a store for all stale and damaged products. D. Handle all store resets for product placement."
  },
  {
    "id": "c009",
    "name": "3(ii)(a)(iii). Prohibited operations",
    "text": "(iii) | During the term of this Agreement, DISTRIBUTOR must not: A. Engage in Wholesaler operations whereby “in-store service” is not provided to individual store outlets. B. Engage in a “bid process” to be awarded a contract for providing specific customers with products for a designated period of time. In addition, DISTRIBUTOR must meet certain other guidelines that the COMPANY may determine in its discretion from time to time."
  },
  {
    "id": "c010",
    "name": "3(ii)(b). Company standards and nonexclusive rights",
    "text": "(b) Without limitation, DISTRIBUTOR shall adhere to the standards, policies, and procedures v (c) (d) as shall from time to time be promulgated, altered, amended or modified by COMPANY. DISTRIBUTOR acknowledges that they do not have exclusive rights to any stores or designated geography. Further, DISTRIBUTOR is prohibited from selling to retail stores serviced by the Kellogg’s Snacks DSD division, or in any channel of trade other than the AUTHORIZED CHANNEL OF TRADE."
  },
  {
    "id": "c011",
    "name": "3(ii)(c). Sales restrictions",
    "text": "TRADE. DISTRIBUTOR shall not sell the PRODUCTS or any of COMPANY’S other products to any CUSTOMERS or in any AUTHORIZED CHANNEL OF TRADE other than as stated herein. Furthermore, DISTRIBUTOR is prohibited from selling to the customers and within the other channels of trade identified on Exhibit “B” attached hereto and incorporated herein. Exhibit “B” may be revised from time to time without notice in the sole discretion of COMPANY, and any such changes are effective thirty days of receipt of changes from COMPANY. In the event DISTRIBUTOR sells any such PRODUCTS or any other products outside of, or in conflict with, the provisions of this Agreement, DISTRIBUTOR shall be considered in breach of this Agreement and subject to termination pursuant to Paragraph 12 herein."
  },
  {
    "id": "c012",
    "name": "3(ii)(d). Third-party sales and disputes",
    "text": "herein. COMPANY cannot and does not guarantee that the PRODUCTS will not be sold to CUSTOMERS in the TERRITORY by persons or entities other than DISTRIBUTOR whether or not in the AUTHORIZED CHANNEL OF TRADE, either by COMPANY through other trade channels, or by distributors or other third parties other than DISTRIBUTOR or otherwise and COMPANY shall have no liability to DISTRIBUTOR for such sales. In the event of sales which are in conflict with Paragraph 3(a)(i) above, however, COMPANY will make commercially reasonable efforts to resolve any conflicts, it being understood that the resolution of any such conflict may, or may not be in the DISTRIBUTOR’S favor. IN THE EVENT THERE IS A DISPUTE CONCERNING THE STATUS OF CERTAIN CUSTOMERS, CHANNELS OF TRADE, OR GEOGRAPHIC AREA, COMPANY’S DECISION IN SUCH MATTERS SHALL BE FINAL AND BINDING ON DISTRIBUTOR."
  },
  {
    "id": "c013",
    "name": "3(ii)(e). Product delivery",
    "text": "(g) During the term of this Agreement, COMPANY shall deliver the PRODUCTS to DISTRIBUTOR for distribution to the CUSTOMERS."
  },
  {
    "id": "c014",
    "name": "3(ii)(f). Force majeure",
    "text": "CUSTOMERS. If performance by COMPANY of any of its duties or obligations under this Agreement is prevented, hindered, delayed or otherwise made impracticable as a result of any cause beyond its control (“force majeure”) and cannot be overcome by reasonable diligence, COMPANY shall be excused from such performance to the extent that it is so prevented, hindered or delayed. COMPANY shall, as soon as reasonably practicable, notify DISTRIBUTOR in writing of the nature and extent of such force majeure, and DISTRIBUTOR shall advise all CUSTOMERS in the TERRITORY accordingly."
  },
  {
    "id": "c015",
    "name": "3(ii)(g). Delivery cancellations and cuts",
    "text": "accordingly. Without limitation of the foregoing, COMPANY reserves the right, in it sole discretion, to cancel at any time any delivery of PRODUCTS, in whole or in part, without liability to DISTRIBUTOR, and COMPANY may, in its sole discretion, designate a decrease in the delivery of PRODUCT to DISTRIBUTOR (“cut”). COMPANY assumes no liability to DISTRIBUTOR for delays in delivery of the PRODUCTS, or from “cuts” or cancellations of orders, and reserves the right to discontinue sale of any item of the PRODUCTS, and to allocate the supply of items of the PRODUCTS, without incurring any liability to Page"
  },
  {
    "id": "c016",
    "name": "3(ii)(h). Company records",
    "text": "DISTRIBUTOR. COMPANY shall maintain records of orders received and accepted, of the PRODUCTS shipped to DISTRIBUTOR, of returns received or substantiated, and of any discounts due."
  },
  {
    "id": "c017",
    "name": "3(ii)(G). Sales calls",
    "text": "due. COMPANY may make such sales calls on chains and other customers within the TERRITORY as, in its sole discretion, may aid in marketing the PRODUCTS."
  },
  {
    "id": "c018",
    "name": "3(ii)(k). Company sales and continuity rights",
    "text": "PRODUCTS. COMPANY reserves the right, in addition to those provided herein, in the exercise of its sole discretion (which shall be final, conclusive and binding upon the parties hereto): (i) within the TERRITORY, to sell and distribute the PRODUCTS or to make other arrangements for the sale and distribution of the PRODUCTS to customers other than the CUSTOMERS; and (ii) to assure continuity in delivery of PRODUCTS to all customers, including the CUSTOMERS; and, if necessary to assure such continuity, the right to deliver to a customer’s or a CUSTOMER’S central or district warehouse."
  },
  {
    "id": "c019",
    "name": "3(ii)(I). Inspection rights",
    "text": "warehouse. Without notice to DISTRIBUTOR, COMPANY shall have the right to inspect (and the right to have its agents and employees inspect) at any time during normal business hours any and all warehouse and equipment maintained and/or used by DISTRIBUTOR in connection with its performance hereunder. COMPANY will make reasonable efforts not to disturb the operations of DISTRIBUTOR during any such inspection. Such right of inspection shall include the right to take physical inventories and inspections of the PRODUCTS."
  },
  {
    "id": "c020",
    "name": "3(ii)(m). Best efforts and competitive products",
    "text": "PRODUCTS. DISTRIBUTOR agrees and covenants to use its best efforts to develop and maximize the sale of the PRODUCTS to the CUSTOMERS in the AUTHORIZED CHANNEL OF TRADE in the TERRITORY and service its CUSTOMERS and TERRITORY in accordance with Good Industry Practice as defined above. DISTRIBUTOR shall refrain from derogating, diminishing or otherwise weakening COMPANY’S rights by engaging in any activities whatsoever in the TERRITORY involving any other products which may reasonably be deemed as injurious to the sales potential of PRODUCTS in the TERRITORY, including sales and promotion of competitive cookie, cracker, and wholesome snack products unless otherwise agreed by mutual written consent of the parties, COMPANY and DISTRIBUTOR hereby agree that DISTRIBUTOR’S sale and promotion of TastyKake and Stella D’oro cake, cookie, cracker and snack products and all other non-cookie or cake snack products (such as potato chips, pretzels, nuts and meat snacks) are specifically authorized by COMPANY and shall not be deemed violative of this subsection “I”. With regard to other products DISTRIBUTOR may sell which may possibly be competitive with COMPANY’S products, DISTRIBUTOR shall notify COMPANY in advance of its intent to sell same and COMPANY shall promptly reply and not unreasonably withheld its consent by unreasonably asserting that any such product is competitive with COMPANY’S products. Products that are from Nabisco or Pepperidge Farms and any companies who are parents, affiliates or subsidiaries with either Nabisco or Pepperidge Farms are competitive with COMPANY’s Products; DISTRIBUTOR agrees not to sell any such products."
  },
  {
    "id": "c021",
    "name": "3(ii)(n). Deliveries to customers",
    "text": "DISTRIBUTOR shall deliver PRODUCTS to the CUSTOMERS: (A) in amounts determined by DISTRIBUTOR and the individual store manager or b\\ a (n) (0) (p) (q) (r) other appropriate person; and (B) in accordance with COMPANY’S policies (as they presently exist and as they may be modified, amended or supplemented from time to time), including the use of such purchase order or other forms as COMPANY may designate and including use of electronic data processing equipment compatible with the system maintained by COMPANY if so requested by COMPANY for billing, route accounting, and /or settlement. DISTRIBUTOR and COMPANY agree to share in the cost of implementing and using any electronic data processing equipment that is required to be used by COMPANY in its sole discretion. COMPANY acknowledges that DISTRIBUTOR has expended sums to acquire hand held electronic data ordering/invoice systems, and COMPANY agrees that - - should it determine to make the use of such equipment mandatory upon its DSDD distributors on or before July 10, 2010 - - then COMPANY shall reimburse DISTRIBUTOR for its prior expenditures for such equipment on such terms and in such amounts as COMPANY reimburses its other DSDD distributors."
  },
  {
    "id": "c022",
    "name": "3(ii)(o). Customer service and stale products",
    "text": "DISTRIBUTOR shall diligently service all CUSTOMERS as necessary to maintain an adequate supply of the PRODUCTS. Any damaged or stale (as indicated expiration date) PRODUCTS will be removed promptly from CUSTOMERS’ stores at DISTRIBUTOR’S sole expense (and not sold) in order to ensure that the PRODUCTS are sold only in a fresh (not stale) state. Upon request of DISTRIBUTOR, COMPANY shall utilize all commercially reasonable efforts to assist DISTRIBUTOR in disposing of DISTRIBUTOR’S “short dated” products (defined as products whose expiration dates are approaching in the near future) prior to their expiration dates provided, however, that DISTRIBUTOR theretofore utilized commercially reasonable efforts to sell such products and further provided that DISTRIBUTOR notifies COMPANY at least 45 days prior to the applicable product expiration dates (if such notification comes within 45 days of such product expiration dates, then COMPANY shall confer with DISTRIBUTOR and, in COMPANY’S sole discretion, COMPANY may assist DISTRIBUTOR in disposing of such short dated products)."
  },
  {
    "id": "c023",
    "name": "3(ii)(p). Service standards",
    "text": "DISTRIBUTOR shall maintain such standards in servicing CUSTOMERS, in sales administration and training, and in accounting for sales, as are conducive to maintenance and furtherance of the reputation and sale of the PRODUCTS, of COMPANY, and of DISTRIBUTOR."
  },
  {
    "id": "c024",
    "name": "3(ii)(q). Credit information assistance",
    "text": "DISTRIBUTOR shall, upon request, assist COMPANY in providing or obtaining information as to the credit standing of itself."
  },
  {
    "id": "c025",
    "name": "3(ii)(r). Distributor personnel",
    "text": "DISTRIBUTOR shall, at its cost and expense, hire, develop, train and supervise its own personnel, under such terms and conditions, as DISTRIBUTOR may deem appropriate. It is specifically understood and agreed, however, that under no circumstances shall any employee, agent, or independent contractor of DISTRIBUTOR be deemed a third party beneficiary to this Agreement, or an employee of COMPANY."
  },
  {
    "id": "c026",
    "name": "3(ii)(s). Expenses and collections",
    "text": "All expenses and disbursements incurred in connection with the solicitation of orders for the PRODUCTS, and/or in connection with the delivery and pick-up of the PRODUCTS, as well as those related to any other activities of DISTRIBUTOR contemplated in this yf (s) (t) (u) (v) Agreement, shall be borne solely by DISTRIBUTOR, unless expressly stated otherwise herein. DISTRIBUTOR is responsible for the collection of all cash sales in the TERRITORY and COMPANY shall have no responsibility to DISTRIBUTOR if the cash cannot be collected in full. DISTRIBUTOR is wholly responsible for collection of accounts receivable with exception for accounts where COMPANY is responsible for accounts receivable (e.g. Kmart)."
  },
  {
    "id": "c027",
    "name": "3(ii)(t). Trucks, personnel and equipment",
    "text": "DISTRIBUTOR is responsible for obtaining its own delivery trucks, personnel, and other equipment necessary to operate its business and to provide the activities contemplated hereunder."
  },
  {
    "id": "c028",
    "name": "3(ii)(u). Truck sanitation and maintenance",
    "text": "DISTRIBUTOR is responsible for truck sanitation and maintenance. Consistent with Good Industry Practice, the delivery trucks shall be kept clean at all times and maintained in such condition as to provide safe, prompt, and regular service to all CUSTOMERS."
  },
  {
    "id": "c029",
    "name": "3(ii)(v). Promotions and indemnification",
    "text": "DISTRIBUTOR shall be solely responsible for any and all promotions, sales and marketing programs, advertising and the like. Under no circumstances will COMPANY be liable for any of DISTRIBUTOR’S obligations, contractual or otherwise, actual or purported, that DISTRIBUTOR may have, or is alleged to have, with any of its employees, agents, subcontractors, independent operators or customers, including the CUSTOMERS, and DISTRIBUTOR hereby indemnifies and holds COMPANY harmless from any and all claims that may arise as a result of any such obligation or alleged obligation."
  },
  {
    "id": "c030",
    "name": "3(ii). Promotional-claims settlement payment",
    "text": "Concurrent with the execution of this Agreement, DISTRIBUTOR shall pay COMPANY the sum of $5,250.71 in full satisfaction of COMPANY’S claimed variance of DISTRIBUTOR’S promotional claims as against COMPANY’S product shipments (as identified by COMPANY in a writing tendered to DISTRIBUTOR on November 14, 2006). Said sum of arrived at as follows: $40,200.71 claimed due by COMPANY minus $4,950.00 owed by COMPANY to DISTRIBUTOR as reimbursement for DISTRIBUTOR advancing costs associated with two retailer golf outings and further minus the approximate $30,000.00 which COMPANY owes DISTRIBUTOR for various credits which are fully accrued, due and owing as of the date hereof."
  },
  {
    "id": "c031",
    "name": "4. PRICES AND TERMS",
    "text": "4, PRICES AND TERMS PRODUCTS will be sold to DISTRIBUTOR at such terms as established by COMPANY from time to time, and DISTRIBUTOR agrees to comply with such terms. COMPANY reserves the right to change the terms upon thirty (30) days written notice to DISTRIBUTOR."
  },
  {
    "id": "c032",
    "name": "4(i). Minimum orders",
    "text": "(i) For all PRODUCTS shipped from a COMPANY DSD Grocery Distribution Center and a COMPANY Non Grocery (NSD) Distribution Center, the minimum order requirement shall be 50 cases per delivery by COMPANY to DISTRIBUTOR. For all PRODUCTS shipped from a COMPANY bakery shipping facility the minimum shipment shall be 250 cases per delivery by COMPANY to DISTRIBUTOR."
  },
  {
    "id": "c033",
    "name": "4(ii). Product price lists",
    "text": "(ii) COMPANY will provide updated PRODUCT price lists as necessary or upon DISTRIBUTOR’S request. COMPANY reserves the right to establish or revise at its sole discretion, from time to time upon thirty (30) days written notice, prices for its sales of PRODUCTS to DISTRIBUTOR, including the right at any time to issue new price lists and to change the prices, and other provisions"
  },
  {
    "id": "c034",
    "name": "4(iii). Title and risk of loss",
    "text": "contained. All PRODUCTS will be sold to DISTRIBUTOR absolutely and the title and risk of loss will pass to DISTRIBUTOR upon delivery to DISTRIBUTOR’S warehouse."
  },
  {
    "id": "c035",
    "name": "4(iv). Promotional Discounts",
    "text": "Definitions and Calculations of DISTRIBUTOR Discounts that may be available from time to time upon written notice from COMPANY: Promotional Discounts also known as Trade Discounts — Dollar (“$”) per case allowances where COMPANY is responsible for seventy-five percent (75%) of the total allowance, and the DISTRIBUTOR is responsible for the remaining twenty-five percent (25%) of the allowance. DISTRIBUTOR is required to pass thru the entire one hundred percent (100%) of the promotional allowance to the CUSTOMER. Such discounts are available from time to time at COMPANY ’S sole discretion. EXAMPLE of Promotional Discount for illustrative purposes only: $30.00 — Case list price to DISTRIBUTOR $6.00 — Total amount of Promotional Discount to be passed through to CUSTOMER $4.50 - COMPANY ’S portion of Promotional Discount (75% of the Promotional Discount) $1.50 - DISTRIBUTOR portion of Promotional Discount (25% of the Promotional Discount)"
  },
  {
    "id": "c036",
    "name": "4(iv). Operating Discount",
    "text": "Operating Discount — this discount is applied to all PRODUCTS purchased by DISTRIBUTOR to offset their handling costs. The “% operating discount,” which may vary by product, is applied to the COMPANY’S list price for the product before any Trade Discounts are applied and shall be deducted from DISTRIBUTOR’S invoice price. The percentage of the operating discount is determined by COMPANY at its sole discretion."
  },
  {
    "id": "c037",
    "name": "4(iv). Cash Discount",
    "text": "Cash Discount ~- DISTRIBUTOR will receive a cash discount if a payment is made within designated number of days the COMPANY has allowed in its current credit terms. The Cash Discount must be applied to the “net invoice” amount, meaning the amount owed by the DISTRIBUTOR after all allowances (e.g. operating discount, Trade Discounts, etc.) have been deducted,"
  },
  {
    "id": "c038",
    "name": "4(v). Payment Terms",
    "text": "Payment Terms. DISTRIBUTOR shall pay net thirty (30) days from the date of receipt for all orders received (35 days if DISTRIBUTOR effects payment by electronic funds transfer). A one percent (1%) discount is allowed for payments made within fifteen (15) days from such date of receipt (20 days if DISTRIBUTOR effects payment by electronic funds transfer),"
  },
  {
    "id": "c039",
    "name": "5(i). Orders for Terminated Product",
    "text": "PLACEMENT OF ORDERS Orders for Terminated Product Termination or elimination of any PRODUCT from the list of PRODUCTS shall have no effect on any orders which may have been issued by DISTRIBUTOR and accepted by COMPANY prior to such termination or elimination and shall not relieve the parties of their obligations under such issued orders."
  },
  {
    "id": "c040",
    "name": "5(ii). Terms contained in Order Forms",
    "text": "Terms contained in Order Forms The terms and conditions on purchase order forms issued by DISTRIBUTOR shall not be deemed to be a part of this Agreement and shall not be deemed to modify or supplement this Agreement in any way, notwithstanding the fact that COMPANY may acknowledge or otherwise approve such purchase orders. This Agreement, and the purchase terms contained herein, may be modified only in accordance with the procedures set forth herein."
  },
  {
    "id": "c041",
    "name": "6. SHIPPING INSTRUCTIONS",
    "text": "SHIPPING INSTRUCTIONS Shipping instructions for PRODUCTS shall be furnished with the orders submitted by DISTRIBUTOR. Such instructions shall call for delivery of PRODUCTS on a scheduled delivery date, which shall not be less than ten (10) business days from COMPANY’S receipt of the instructions. COMPANY shall ship or arrange for shipment so that the ordered PRODUCTS will be available to DISTRIBUTOR on the scheduled delivery date, plus or minus five (5) business days; provided, however, that if an ordered item(s) is not in stock DISTRIBUTOR shall have the option of reordering the item(s) at a later date. DISTRIBUTOR shall designate a location for delivery of the PRODUCTS acceptable to COMPANY, which will be of suitable size for COMPANY’S delivery trucks and with the necessary loading dock heights to allow for use by COMPANY. DISTRIBUTOR shall be responsible for handling and storage of PRODUCTS after delivery."
  },
  {
    "id": "c042",
    "name": "7(i). Inspection",
    "text": "ACCEPTANCE AND CLAIMS Inspection All PRODUCTS shall be received subject to DISTRIBUTOR’S inspection and may be rejected as provided in this Agreement if found not to conform to the guarantee set forth in Paragraph 8 herein or any quality, and/or grade requirements agreed to in writing between the parties. COMPANY reserves the right to replace PRODUCTS or provide credit, as provided in this Paragraph, and DISTRIBUTOR agrees that this is its sole remedy for any violation of the guarantee set forth in Paragraph 8."
  },
  {
    "id": "c043",
    "name": "7(ii). Report of Claims",
    "text": "Report of Claims All claims for alleged nonconforming PRODUCTS which may be discovered by inspection, or shortages, shall be reported, via email, facsimile, and/or in writing, to COMPANY as soon as possible, but no later than 24 hours after becoming aware of such claims."
  },
  {
    "id": "c044",
    "name": "7(iii). Evidence of Defect/Credit for Returned Product",
    "text": "(iii) | Evidence of Defect/Credit for Returned Product At COMPANY'S request, DISTRIBUTOR shall promptly supply either some of the units of the allegedly nonconforming PRODUCTS or some other evidence of deficiency which COMPANY shall specify, including but not limited to products received with less than sixty (60) days of remaining shelf life at the time of delivery. Credit for nonconforming PRODUCTS shall be issued upon COMPANY'S confirmation of DISTRIBUTOR'S claims. Returns of PRODUCTS shall qualify for credit in accordance with policies and standards set and established from time to time by COMPANY and communicated to DISTRIBUTOR. Returns, which do not meet such policies and procedures, shall not qualify and shall be denied credit."
  },
  {
    "id": "c045",
    "name": "7(iv). Product Replacement",
    "text": "(iv) Product Replacement COMPANY reserves the right, at its choice and discretion, to replace PRODUCTS found to be nonconforming or short in quantity with such quantity of PRODUCTS in good, saleable condition to satisfy DISTRIBUTOR'S purchase requirements, delivering such replacements to DISTRIBUTOR’S warehouse at COMPANY'S expense, or to issue a credit to DISTRIBUTOR for the prorated invoice amount plus such documented costs and expenses incurred in situating unsaleable PRODUCTS in DISTRIBUTOR’S warehouse."
  },
  {
    "id": "c046",
    "name": "7(v). Disposition of Non-Conforming Product",
    "text": "(v) Disposition of Non-Conforming Product COMPANY also reserves the right to require DISTRIBUTOR to return to COMPANY all or part of any nonconforming PRODUCTS, destroy them or otherwise dispose of them at COMPANY'S expense and pursuant to COMPANY’S instructions."
  },
  {
    "id": "c047",
    "name": "8. COMPANY GUARANTEE",
    "text": "8. COMPANY GUARANTEE COMPANY guarantees that no PRODUCTS comprising any shipments or deliveries hereafter made by COMPANY to DISTRIBUTOR shall be, as of the date of such shipments or deliveries, adulterated or misbranded within the meaning of the United States Federal Food, Drug, and Cosmetic Act, and all revisions and amendments pertaining thereto, or within the meaning of any Food and Drug Law effective within the TERRITORY the adulteration and misbranding provisions of which are identical with, or substantially the same as, those found in the United States Federal Act; provided, however, that COMPANY does not guarantee against such PRODUCTS becoming adulterated or misbranded within the meaning of said Act after shipment, by reason of causes beyond COMPANY'S control; provided, also, that where PRODUCTS are manufactured by DISTRIBUTOR and shipped under DISTRIBUTOR'S labels, the guarantee provided for hereunder shall not apply and COMPANY shall have no responsibility whatsoever, except for patent and trademark rights granted by COMPANY to DISTRIBUTOR."
  },
  {
    "id": "c048",
    "name": "9. TRADEMARK AND PATENT PROTECTION",
    "text": "9, TRADEMARK AND PATENT PROTECTION All trademarks, trade names, logos, and other designations used or adopted by COMPANY in connection with PRODUCTS (the “Trademarks”) will at all times be and remain the property of COMPANY (or its affiliated entities). DISTRIBUTOR will sell PRODUCTS in the packaging supplied by COMPANY and will comply with all instructions of COMPANY (or its affiliates) with regard to use and display of the Trademarks, DISTRIBUTOR shall at all times recognize, respect, and protect COMPANY ’S (or its affiliates’) right to total ownership of any and all trademarks and patents in connection with PRODUCTS in the TERRITORY and shall not in any way derogate, diminish, or weaken COMPANY’S (or its affiliates’) property rights in said registrations."
  },
  {
    "id": "c049",
    "name": "10(i). Supplied by Company",
    "text": "INFORMATION, DATA AND MATERIALS Supplied by Company Unless otherwise specifically agreed, COMPANY shall supply DISTRIBUTOR, at COMPANY’S sole discretion, with the following information, data and material on PRODUCTS as may be available to COMPANY: (a) Market information; (b) Commercial product literature in reasonable quantities; (c) Information on improvements made on any PRODUCT; (d) Such other promotional information and assistance as may be available from time to time, including sales instruction, and equipment such as trays, racks, bins and the like. All such information and/or equipment supplied by COMPANY shall be and remains the property of COMPANY and shall be returned to COMPANY when requested or upon termination of this Agreement. In the case of equipment, COMPANY may, at its sole discretion, require and withhold from DISTRIBUTOR, a reasonable sum to assure return or replacement of equipment."
  },
  {
    "id": "c050",
    "name": "10(ii). Promotional Material",
    "text": "Promotional Material DISTRIBUTOR shall refrain from using any packing materials, descriptive literature, advertising, etc., pertaining to PRODUCTS without COMPANY'S prior written consent. Unless otherwise specifically agreed, DISTRIBUTOR shall include COMPANY'S trademarks associated with PRODUCTS and COMPANY'S name and address as supplier of PRODUCTS on all packaging, promotional materials, write-ups, and the like, relating to PRODUCTS."
  },
  {
    "id": "c051",
    "name": "10(iii). Supplied by DISTRIBUTOR",
    "text": "Supplied by DISTRIBUTOR DISTRIBUTOR shall supply upon COMPANY ’S request the General market information regarding the TERRITORY."
  },
  {
    "id": "c052",
    "name": "11. CONFIDENTIAL INFORMATION",
    "text": "CONFIDENTIAL INFORMATION DISTRIBUTOR shall maintain in strict confidence and take all necessary steps and measures to safeguard any and all business and technical information pertaining to the COMPANY and/or the PRODUCTS and shall not, at any time, disclose such information to others or make use of such information in ways not permitted by this Agreement. Confidential information includes but is not limited to any materials provided by COMPANY to DISTRIBUTOR under Sections 10(i) and 10(ii)."
  },
  {
    "id": "c053",
    "name": "12(i). Termination on notice",
    "text": "12, (i) TERMINATION This Agreement may be terminated by either party at any time upon ninety (90) days written notice to the other for good cause (defined as either party’s breach of this Agreement which is not cured within those times specified below) or a change in COMPANY ’s business that results in COMPANY no longer using Independent DSDD distributors in this territory, with the date of yf (il) (ili) termination to be set forth in the notice or by mutual agreement."
  },
  {
    "id": "c054",
    "name": "12(ii). Immediate termination",
    "text": "This Agreement may be terminated immediately by COMPANY if DISTRIBUTOR should: (a) (b) (c) (d) (e) (f) Attempt to assign, convey or otherwise transfer, in whole or in part, any of DISTRIBUTOR'S rights hereunder to any third party without COMPANY'S express prior written consent, which consent shall not be unreasonably withheld; Make a material change in the control of DISTRIBUTOR’S company that is unacceptable to COMPANY; Cease to function as a going concern or conduct its operation as a distributor; Become involved in financial difficulties requiring the appointment of a receiver or the like, or a moratorium on indebtedness or petition in bankruptcy or the like filed by or against DISTRIBUTOR or an assignment on behalf of DISTRIBUTOR'S creditors; Submit fraudulent reports or information or continue to submit false or untrue reports or information to Company; Commit a failure of performance that involves criminal activity, threatens the public health or safety or threatens to do substantial harm to the COMPANY’S business or commercial reputation."
  },
  {
    "id": "c055",
    "name": "12(iii)(a). Curable payment or unauthorized-sales breach",
    "text": "Curable Breach (a) (b) In the event DISTRIBUTOR fails to pay for Product when due in accordance with Paragraph 4; or sells PRODUCT outside of DISTRIBUTOR’S AUTHORIZED CHANNEL OF TRADE; COMPANY shall give DISTRIBUTOR five (5) business days written notice within which DISTRIBUTOR may cure its failure of performance by making all payments due, and may cure unauthorized selling by ceasing to sell to unauthorized customers. If DISTRIBUTOR fails to cure such failure of performance within said five (5) day period, COMPANY may thereafter terminate this Agreement and DISTRIBUTOR will have no further right to cure; provided, further, that the parties agree that should any such failure(s) occur more than two (2) times during any twelve (12) month period, COMPANY may immediately terminate this Agreement upon written notice to DISTRIBUTOR and DISTRIBUTOR will have no further right to cure."
  },
  {
    "id": "c056",
    "name": "12(iii)(b). Other curable breach",
    "text": "In the event of a failure to perform hereunder not otherwise set forth in (i), (ii), or (iti) (a) above including, but not limited to, DISTRIBUTOR’S failure to operate its business in accordance with Good Industry Practice, failure to comply with or to perform any of its duties or obligations hereunder, which, in the sole discretion of COMPANY, are material to the Agreement or to the operation of COMPANY’S business; or failure to regularly service CUSTOMERS and remove out-of-date merchandise from CUSTOMERS’ shelves, then COMPANY shall give DISTRIBUTOR five (5) business days written notice within which DISTRIBUTOR may cure its failure to perform. If DISTRIBUTOR fails to cure such failure of performance within said five (5) day period (or within such longer, commercially reasonable period of time if the breach, by its nature, is not capable of being cured within five (5) days, in which circumstance DISTRIBUTOR shall use its best efforts to cure the breach at the earliest commercially reasonable time), COMPANY may thereafter terminate this Agreement and DISTRIBUTOR shall have no further right to cure; provided, further, that the parties agree that should any such failure(s) occur more than two (2) times during any twelve (12) month period, ( DISTRIBUTOR’S isolated, but not systemic, curable failures to remove out-of-date merchandise from customers’ shelves is B\\ a (iv) (v) (vi) (vii) 13. (i) not cause for immediate termination unless it occurs more than six (6) times in any twelve (12) month period ), COMPANY may immediately terminate this Agreement upon written notice to DISTRIBUTOR and DISTRIBUTOR will have no further right to cure."
  },
  {
    "id": "c057",
    "name": "12(iv). Repurchase Option",
    "text": "Repurchase Option Within thirty (30) days after expiration or termination of this Agreement, COMPANY may, at its option, repurchase from DISTRIBUTOR, at DISTRIBUTOR'S net warehouse cost, any and all PRODUCTS that are commercially usable or saleable with at least sixty (60) days of code life remaining as well as any usable advertising and/or promotional materials previously purchased by DISTRIBUTOR, with it being understood that COMPANY may repossess (pursuant to Paragraph 12(vi)) without payment any PRODUCTS or items which have not been fully paid for.). DISTRIBUTOR shall make available to COMPANY, free of charge, any and all PRODUCTS, packaging, components, sales promotional materials, and the like, which COMPANY previously made available to DISTRIBUTOR at no charge."
  },
  {
