    "name": "12(v). Damages caused by Termination or Expiration; LIMITATION ON LIABILITY",
    "text": "Damages caused by Termination or Expiration; LIMITATION ON LIABILITY Neither party to this Agreement shall be liable by reason of termination or expiration of this Agreement to the other for compensation, reimbursement or damages on account of any consequential, punitive or incidental damages, such as loss of prospective profits on anticipated sales or on account of expenditures, investments, leases or other commitments relating to the business or goodwill of either party, in any cumulative amount greater than the sum of 50% of DISTRIBUTOR‘S aggregate gross sales of COMPANY’S products in the twelve months immediately preceding the date upon which an action or proceeding is commenced."
  },
  {
    "id": "c059",
    "name": "12(vi). Rights of a Secured Creditor",
    "text": "Rights of a Secured Creditor To secure the payment of any indebtedness or liability of DISTRIBUTOR to COMPANY, now or hereafter arising, DISTRIBUTOR hereby grants and conveys to COMPANY a security interest in all PRODUCTS and related items (such as packaging, components, sales promotional materials) in DISTRIBUTOR’S possession, and grants to COMPANY the rights of a secured party under the Uniform Commercial Code. DISTRIBUTOR, in particular, hereby authorizes and gives its irrevocable consent to the COMPANY (and its employees and agents) to enter into DISTRIBUTOR’S facilities and property for the purpose of repossessing such PRODUCTS and related items, without the need for any further consent or notice."
  },
  {
