  },
  {
    "id": "c065",
    "name": "15(ii)(a). Distributor assignment",
    "text": "(ii) Assignment (a) COMPANY regards DISTRIBUTOR’S services hereunder as personal to DISTRIBUTOR, and DISTRIBUTOR accepts and acknowledges this circumstance. DISTRIBUTOR shall not have the right or power to assign this Agreement, in whole or in part, whether by its affirmative act or by operation of law, and any attempted assignment shall be void and without effect, other than an assignment effected with our prior written consent under the b\\ a terms and conditions hereinafter set forth. Any other attempted assignment by DISTRIBUTOR of this Agreement or any part hereof shall constitute a material breach of this Agreement. DISTRIBUTOR may not sell or otherwise assign or transfer this Agreement, in whole or in part, without COMPANY’s prior written consent. COMPANY will not unreasonably withhold or delay consent to any such assignment or sale provided, however, DISTRIBUTOR agrees that it will not be unreasonable for COMPANY to impose, among other requirements, the following conditions to consenting to the assignment, or to reject the proposed assignee according to COMPANY’s standards for evaluating prospective distributors ; L That the proposed assignee applies to COMPANY for acceptance as a distributor, and furnishes to COMPANY the information and references that COMPANY requests to determine the proposed assignee's skills, qualifications, financial condition, background and history, reputation, economic resources and ability to assume DISTRIBUTOR’s duties and obligations under this Agreement and any related agreement. 2 That the proposed assignee (or, if an entity, the principals of the proposed assignee) presents himself for a personal interview at any location COMPANY designates, at the date and time we reasonably request, without expense to COMPANY. 3. That the assignee (or the principal officers, shareholders or directors of a corporate assignee, or if any other entity, the principals of the assignee entity) demonstrates that he has the skills, qualifications, ethics, moral values and economic resources necessary, in COMPANY’s reasonable judgment, to conduct the business contemplated by this Agreement, and to fulfill its obligations to the assignor. 4, That as of the date of the assignment, DISTRIBUTOR has cured any existing defaults under any provisions of this Agreement and any other agreement or arrangement with COMPANY or it’s affiliates, and have fully satisfied all of DISTRIBUTOR’s accrued monetary and other obligations to COMPANY and it’s affiliates under this Agreement and any other agreement or arrangement with COMPANY or it’s affiliates. Dy That the assignee executes a separate Kellogg Snacks DSDD Agreement in the form and on the terms and conditions then offered to similarly situated distributors. The execution of the new Kellogg Snacks DSDD Agreement will terminate this Agreement, except for DISTRIBUTOR’s guarantees and the posttermination and post-expiration provisions under this Agreement. 6. That the DISTRIBUTOR (and all shareholders of a corporate assignor, and all partners of a partnership assignor, all proprietors of a proprietorship assignor and all shareholders of the general partner of a limited partnership assignor) executes a general release of any and all claims, demands and causes of action which COMPANY and it’s partners, proprietors, directors, officers, shareholders, Nd (iii) (iv) (v) executors, administrators and assigns (as the case may be) may or might have against COMPANY and it’s affiliates, and their respective officers, directors, shareholders, agents, attorneys, contractors and employees in their corporate and individual capacities including, without limitation, claims arising under federal, state and local laws, rules and ordinances. if That DISTRIBUTOR remains liable for all the obligations to COMPANY arising out of or related to this Agreement before the effective date of the transfer or assignment, and executes all instruments reasonably requested by us to evidence this liability. 8, That DISTRIBUTOR does not represent to the proposed assignee that they are purchasing anything beyond the rights to sign a new DSDD agreement with COMPANY. Nothing in this Agreement shall prohibit DISTRIBUTOR from conducting business through subdistributors it may engage provided, however, that each such subdistributor (sometimes referred to as an “independent distributor”) executes and returns to COMPANY that form of “DSDD Indemnification” annexed hereto as Exhibit “C”."
  },
  {
    "id": "c066",
    "name": "15(ii)(b). Company assignment",
    "text": "(b) COMPANY may assign this Agreement or any right or obligation arising hereunder to any affiliate, subsidiary, parent or division of COMPANY without DISTRIBUTOR’S consent."
  },
  {
    "id": "c067",
    "name": "15(iii). Modification",
    "text": "Modification This Agreement may be modified, amended or revised only by a written instrument duly executed by the parties hereto."
  },
  {
    "id": "c068",
    "name": "15(iv). DISTRIBUTOR non agency relationship with Company",
    "text": "DISTRIBUTOR non agency relationship with Company Neither COMPANY nor DISTRIBUTOR shall have any authority to employ any person on behalf of the other. Each party shall have (as between the parties) the exclusive right to select, engage, fix the compensation of, discharge, and otherwise to manage, supervise, and control the person hired by it and shall, with respect to all such persons, perform all obligations and discharge all liabilities imposed upon employers under any governing law or regulation. Without limitation, DISTRIBUTOR: (a) shall be solely responsible for the conduct, direction, and operation of its activities, including but not limited to the conduct, direction, and operation of the activities of its employees and subcontractors, in connection with its business and the performance of its obligations under this Agreement; (b) shall make no contract, representation or warranty nor incur any obligation for or in the name of or binding upon COMPANY and shall not list its place of business as COMPANY’S office but only may identify itself as COMPANY’S independent contractor for the distribution of the PRODUCTS; (c) shall provide and maintain at its own expense suitable equipment for the delivery of the PRODUCTS; (d) shall not pledge COMPANY’S credit or extend credit in COMPANY’S name; and (e) shall indemnify and defend COMPANY against, and save it harmless from, any claims which may arise as a result of any representation by DISTRIBUTOR that it has authority to act on behalf of COMPANY or to bind COMPANY to any obligations whatsoever."
  },
  {
    "id": "c069",
    "name": "15(vi). Choice of Law",
    "text": "(vi) Choice of Law This Agreement will be governed by, and construed under, the laws of the State of Delaware."
  },
  {
    "id": "c070",
    "name": "15(vii). Entire Agreement",
    "text": "(vii) Entire Agreement This Agreement, along with any exhibits and duly executed addenda thereto, shall be deemed to contain the entire and only agreement between the parties relating to the subject matter thereof, and any representations, terms or conditions relating thereto and not incorporated herein shall not be binding upon either party. This Agreement wholly cancels, voids, and supersedes any agreement heretofore entered into between the parties with respect to the subject matter hereof, except as otherwise expressly provided herein."
  },
  {
    "id": "c071",
    "name": "15(viii). Execution",
    "text": "(viii) Execution This Agreement may be executed by duly authorized officers of the respective parties hereto in any number of counterparts, each of which shall be deemed the original."
  },
  {
    "id": "c072",
    "name": "Exhibit A — Territory",
    "text": "Territory v Territory for DISTRIBUTOR: Py, N'T) PA, Cann. , excluding all customers and channels of trade set forth on attached Exhibit B."
  },
  {
    "id": "c073",
    "name": "Exhibit B — Excluded Channels of Trade",
    "text": "4 EXCLUDED CHANNELS OF TRADE Territory and Customers shall not include the list of Channels of Trade unless authorized by COMPANY (as may be amended in COMPANY’S sole discretion from time to time): Mass merchandisers (e.g., Target and Wal-Mart); DISTRIBUTOR may distribute to Kmart under this Agreement. Club stores (e.g., BJ's Wholesale and Costco); Mass market home stores (e.g., Home Depot and Lowe’s); Mass market auto stores (e.g., Auto Zone and Advance Auto Parts); Mass market toy stores (e.g., Toys “R” Us and K-B Toys); Specialty toy stores (whether independent or chain); Mid tier stores (e.g., JC Penney, Kohl's and Sears); Department stores (e.g., May Company and Macy's); Drug stores (whether independent or chain); Convenience stores (whether independent or chain); Liquor stores (whether independent or chain); Book stores and college bookstores (whether independent or chain); Specialty stores (including airport stores and military exchange stores, whether independent or chain); Specialty domestics retailers (whether independent or chain); Office supply stores (whether independent or chain); Party supply stores (whether independent or chain); Electronics stores (whether independent or chain); Card and gift stores (whether independent or chain); Gift stores (whether independent or chain); Stationery stores (whether independent or chain); Arts and craft stores (whether independent or chain); Music stores (whether independent or chain); Video stores (whether independent or chain); Comic book stores (whether independent or chain); Retailers known in the industry or classified as so-called \"99 cent\", “value discount stores”, \"dollar stores\" or liquidator\" stores Chain Warehouse programs Limited Assortment Discounters (e.g. Save-A-Lot, Aldi)"
  },
  {
    "id": "c074",
    "name": "Exhibit B — Existing-customer exception",
    "text": "Notwithstanding the foregoing, until further notice from COMPANY it shall be permissible for DISTRIBUTOR to continue selling products to, and servicing, any of its customers as of the date hereof who fall within the above schedule."
  },
  {
    "id": "c075",
    "name": "Exhibit C — Independent distributor relationship",
    "text": "The undersigned independent distributor (hereafter, “Ind.Distr.”) hereby acknowledges and agrees that, except to the extent expressly set forth herein, there exists no relationship of any kind, contractual or otherwise, between Ind.Distr. and KELLOGG SALES COMPANY D/B/A KELLOGG SNACKS (hereinafter “Kellogg”) and that any and all rights Ind.Distr. may have relating to the purchase, distribution, and/or sale of Kellogg products (hereinafter “Products”) are derived solely from TWO LOCKS, INC. d/b/a PREMIER SNACK DISTRIBUTORS (hereinafter “Premier”) pursuant to any agreement or understanding that may from time-to-time be in effect by and between Premier and Ind.Distr.. Ind.Distr. shall not represent that it holds any interest in Kellogg nor that it is in an agent or partner of Kellogg. No employee or agent of Ind.Distr. shall, as an employee or agent of Ind.Distr., be considered or deemed in any way to be an employee or agent of Kellogg. No agreement or relationship existing between Ind.Distr. and Premier shall be construed as constituting Ind.Distr. as a partner or agent of Kellogg or as creating a relationship of employer-employee, franchisor, franchisee, or principal-agent between Ind.Distr. and Kellogg."
  },
  {
    "id": "c076",
    "name": "Exhibit C — Intellectual property protection",
    "text": "Ind.Distr. shall at all times recognize, respect, and protect Kellogg’s rights of total ownership of any and al trademarks, patents, and/or other intellectual property rights associated with the Products and shall not take any action, nor fail to take any actions, that has the effect, as determined by Kellogg in its sole and absolute discretion, of derogating, diminishing and/or weakening Kellogg’s rights in any such trademark, patent, and/or other intellectual property right, including, but not limited to, any actual or attempted utilization by Ind.Distr. of any Kellogg trademark, patent, and/or other intellectual property right in connection with the purchase, distribution, and/or sale of any goods other than those manufactured, produced, or sold by Kellogg."
  },
  {
    "id": "c077",
    "name": "Exhibit C — Direct distributions and sales",
    "text": "Ind.Distr. hereby acknowledges that Kellogg may, from time-to-time engage in direct distributions and/or sales of Products or other goods produced, manufactured, distributed, and/or sold by Kellogg to customers and/or potential customers of Ind.Distr. to the extent permitted by the agreement then in effect between Kellogg and Premier. In such event Ind.Distr. acknowledges and agrees that it shall have no right or cause of action against Kellogg."
  },
  {
    "id": "c078",
    "name": "Exhibit C — Product and relationship changes",
    "text": "Ind.Distr. hereby acknowledges that Kellogg may, from time-to-time, add to, delete from, alter, modify, and/or otherwise change the composition of the goods constitution Products it sells to Premier, which Premier may subsequently sell to Ind.Distr., and/or that Kellogg and/or Premier may otherwise alter or terminate the business relationship between them. In any such event, Ind.Distr. acknowledges and agrees that it shall have no right or cause of action against Kellogg."
  },
  {
    "id": "c079",
    "name": "Exhibit C — No third-party beneficiary status",
