  {"clause_id": "c059", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The security interest and irrevocable self-help entry right extend to \"all PRODUCTS and related items ... in DISTRIBUTOR'S possession,\" including goods already sold to DISTRIBUTOR absolutely with title passing under Section 4(iii). Whether COMPANY may repossess goods it no longer owns, and without notice, would have to be construed against that provision.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.18}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c060", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The two-year period runs from when \"the harm that gave rise to the cause of action arose,\" which is not the same as accrual and may precede the claimant's knowledge of it. When the clock starts for a continuing course of conduct, such as ongoing under-delivery or territorial encroachment, is left open.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.38}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c061", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The mutual indemnity covers claims \"caused or alleged to be caused, by a breach of this Agreement by\" the indemnifying party, without saying whether it reaches first-party claims between COMPANY and DISTRIBUTOR or only third-party claims. Read the first way it would let a party recover its attorneys' fees for the other's breach.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.26}
